{title: O Day of Peace That Dimly Shines}
{key: C}
{time: 3/2}

{start_of_verse: 1}
O [C]day of [Am]peace[**] that [F]dimly [C]shines[**]
[F]Through all our [C]hopes and [Dm]prayers [**]and [F]dreams[**]
Guide [C]us to [Am]jus[**]-tice, [Em]truth, and [Am]love[**]
De[Em]livered [Am]from our [G]sel[D]fish [G]schemes[**]
May [G]swords of [Dm]hate[**] fall [G]from our [Dm]hands[**]
Our [Dm]hearts from [F]en[**]-vy [Gm]find re[F]lease[**]
Till [F]by God's [Dm]grace[**] our [G]warring [C]world[**]
Shall [Am]see Christ's [F]promised [C]reign [G]of [C]peace[**].
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Then [C]shall the [Am]wolf[**] dwell [F]with the [C]lambs[**]
[F]Nor shall the [C]fierce de[Dm]vour [**]the [F]small[**]
As [C]beasts and [Am]ca[**]-ttle [Em]calmly [Am]graze[**]
A [Em]little [Am]child shall [G]lead [D]them [G]all[**]
Then [G]ene[Dm]mies[**] shall [G]learn to [Dm]love[**]
All [Dm]creatures [F]find[**] their [Gm]true ac[F]cord[**]
The [F]hope of [Dm]peace[**] shall [G]be ful[C]filled[**]
For [Am]all the [F]earth shall [C]know [G]the [C]Lord[**].
{end_of_verse}
